foundation.question_text:
How many straws and joiners are needed for a skeletal model of this triangular prism?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.3,2);
\coordinate (D) at (1.1,0.7);
\coordinate (E) at (3.7,0.7);
\coordinate (F) at (2.4,2.7);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (B)--(E)--(F)--(C);
\draw (C)--(F);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(D)--(E);
\draw[dashed] (D)--(F);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many straws and joiners are needed for a skeletal model of this square pyramid?
